% 7 U.S.C. 2014(g) — us:statutes/7/2014/g
the text of "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/g.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(B)(i)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/g.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/g.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/g.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(C)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/g.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv); 7 USC 2014(g)(2)(C); 7 USC 2014(g)(2)(D)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/g.yaml".

rule snap_household_resource_limit_base_amount with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(A)":
the snap household resource limit base amount is 2000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule snap_household_resource_limit_base_amount_with_elderly_or_disabled_member with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(A)":
the snap household resource limit base amount with elderly or disabled member is 3000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule allowable_financial_resources_rounding_increment with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(B)(i)":
the allowable financial resources rounding increment is 250 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule statutory_household_resource_limit_base_amount with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(A)":
the statutory household resource limit base amount of a household is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the household includes elderly or disabled member
        and the snap household resource limit base amount with elderly or disabled member is the amount
        otherwise the household is a household
        and the snap household resource limit base amount is the amount.

rule next_annual_household_resource_limit_amount with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(1)(B)":
the next annual household resource limit amount of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the prior unrounded household resource limit amount of the household is an amount M
    and the consumer price index change for 12 month period ending preceding june of the household is a number K
    and the allowable financial resources rounding increment is an amount P
    and N = floor(M * (1 + K) / P) * P.

rule licensed_vehicle_resource_fair_market_value_threshold with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv)":
the licensed vehicle resource fair market value threshold is 4650 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule vehicle_excluded_from_financial_resources_under_vehicle_exceptions_1 with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(C)":
an asset is vehicle excluded from financial resources under vehicle exceptions if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the asset is vehicle used to produce earned income.

rule vehicle_excluded_from_financial_resources_under_vehicle_exceptions_2 with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(C)":
an asset is vehicle excluded from financial resources under vehicle exceptions if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the asset is vehicle necessary for transport of physically disabled household member.

rule vehicle_excluded_from_financial_resources_under_vehicle_exceptions_3 with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(C)":
an asset is vehicle excluded from financial resources under vehicle exceptions if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the asset is vehicle depended on to carry household fuel or water
    and the vehicle of the asset provides household primary source of fuel or water.

rule licensed_vehicle_countable_resource_amount_under_default_rule with provenance "7 USC 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv); 7 USC 2014(g)(2)(C); 7 USC 2014(g)(2)(D)":
the licensed vehicle countable resource amount under default rule of an asset is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the asset is licensed vehicle
        and the asset is used for household transportation or to obtain or continue employment
        and it is not the case that the asset is vehicle excluded from financial resources under vehicle exceptions
        and it is not the case that the asset is state vehicle allowance standards apply in lieu of default vehicle rule
        and the asset fair market value of the asset is an amount M
        and the licensed vehicle resource fair market value threshold is an amount K
        and M > K
        and the asset fair market value of the asset is an amount P
        and the licensed vehicle resource fair market value threshold is an amount Q
        and N = P - Q
        otherwise the asset is an asset
        and N = 0.

